{
  "comment": [
    "The rider and the bicycle, as measurements rather than as code.",
    "",
    "Everything drawn is built from these: the frame is a list of tubes between",
    "points in the bicycle's side plane, the rider is a set of joints, and each",
    "An arm is 0.59 m from shoulder to wrist and a rider's hands are 0.40 m",
    "from their shoulders, so the elbow is well bent - which is why it is a",
    "joint here and not a straight line.",
    "posture says where the shoulders and the hands go on a particular bicycle.",
    "Change a number here and the figure changes; no code knows any of them.",
    "",
    "Distances are metres, measured from the bottom bracket - the axis the",
    "cranks turn on - with x along the bike and z up. That is the origin a",
    "bicycle is actually built around, and the one that puts the wheels on the",
    "road rather than through it."
  ],
